import LegalLayout from '@/layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="SMS / Messaging Policy"
  description="How Trackwise uses SMS, what consent looks like, and how to opt out. Required disclosures for U.S. A2P 10DLC and Toll-Free Verification."
  eyebrow="Messaging"
  effective="2026-05-17"
  lastUpdated="2026-05-17"
>
  <p>
    This SMS / Messaging Policy explains how <strong>Trackwise LLC</strong>
    uses SMS, how consent is collected, what messages we send, and how to opt
    out. This Policy applies to U.S. recipients and is provided for
    transparency to carriers and reviewers, including the Twilio Trust Hub.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    Trackwise LLC, a Wyoming limited liability company, FinCEN MSB
    #31000299058422, headquartered at 30 N. Gould St., Ste R, Sheridan, WY
    82801, USA. Trackwise sends SMS for the purpose of operating its banking
    infrastructure for fintech businesses.
  </p>

  <h2>2. What we send</h2>
  <p>Trackwise sends three categories of SMS, all transactional:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Account verification (OTP / 2FA).</strong> One-time passcodes for login, password reset, device approval, and step-up authentication.</li>
    <li><strong>Transactional alerts.</strong> Confirmations of transactions, transfers, payments, and account events you initiated.</li>
    <li><strong>Fraud and security notifications.</strong> Warnings about suspicious activity, login from a new device or location, and similar safety events.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>We do not send marketing SMS.</strong> We do not send promotional
    messages, sweepstakes, or third-party advertisements.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Sample messages</h2>
  <p>OTP / 2FA:</p>
  <p><code>Trackwise: 482910 is your verification code. Do not share. Reply STOP to opt out.</code></p>
  <p>Transactional:</p>
  <p><code>Trackwise: $250.00 USD sent to recipient ending ••••4421. Reply STOP to opt out.</code></p>
  <p>Fraud notification:</p>
  <p><code>Trackwise alert: Login attempt from Lima, PE. If this wasn't you, secure your account at trackwise.finance/security. Reply STOP to opt out.</code></p>

  <h2>4. Consent</h2>
  <p>
    Consent is collected on the platform at the time you provide your phone
    number. The consent checkbox is <strong>unchecked by default</strong> and
    must be affirmatively checked by you. The consent language reads:
  </p>
  <p>
    <em>"I agree to receive SMS messages from Trackwise for account verification,
    login, and transactional alerts at the phone number I provided. Message and
    data rates may apply. Frequency varies. Reply STOP to opt out at any time.
    Reply HELP for help. Trackwise does not share or sell SMS opt-in data or
    consent to third parties for marketing."</em>
  </p>
  <p>
    The consent checkbox is visible on the public contact form at{' '}
    <a href="/contact">trackwise.finance/contact</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Frequency</h2>
  <p>
    Frequency varies based on your activity. OTP messages are sent when you
    request authentication. Transactional and fraud alerts are sent only when
    triggered by your account activity. Typical frequency is fewer than five
    (5) messages per session.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Opt-out</h2>
  <p>
    Reply <code>STOP</code>, <code>STOPALL</code>, <code>UNSUBSCRIBE</code>,
    <code>CANCEL</code>, <code>END</code>, or <code>QUIT</code> to any SMS
    from Trackwise to opt out. We will send one confirmation reply and will
    not send further messages, except for transactional messages legally
    required to operate your account.
  </p>
  <p>
    Reply <code>HELP</code> to receive contact information for support.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Sharing of consent data</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Trackwise does not share, sell, rent, or otherwise transfer SMS
    opt-in data or consent to third parties for marketing.</strong> SMS phone
    numbers and consent records are shared only with our messaging carrier
    (Twilio Inc. or a successor) strictly to deliver the requested messages,
    and with regulators or law enforcement where required by law.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Carrier disclaimer</h2>
  <p>
    Message and data rates may apply. Carriers, including T-Mobile, AT&amp;T,
    Verizon, and other U.S. carriers, are not liable for delayed or
    undelivered messages.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    Phone numbers and message metadata are processed in accordance with our{' '}
    <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>, including the <strong>Mobile
    Information and SMS</strong> section.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    For questions about this Policy, email{' '}
    <a href="mailto:support@trackwise.finance">support@trackwise.finance</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
